+ ### Missing or wrong credentials on a returning customer
+ If the agent has no memory of credentials for this email (new device, new session) or the stored values are stale:
+   "status": "credentials_required",
+   "sessionId": "cs_test_new...",
+   "message": "This email has a saved card, but auto-charge requires the customer username and password. Ask the customer to complete this checkout URL to confirm identity, then call claim_credentials..."
+ **Agent:** "Your card is on file, but I need you to re-verify with a quick Stripe checkout so I can charge automatically for you going forward. Click this link: https://checkout.stripe.com/pay/cs_test_..."
+ After the customer pays, call `claim_credentials` with the new `sessionId` and overwrite the stored credentials in memory.
+ ### Lost credentials
+ If the customer's username and password aren't in memory (new device, wiped session), don't ask the customer to recite them — they were saved silently and the customer was never shown them. Just run `initiate_booking` without credentials; the server will return `credentials_required` with a fresh checkout URL, the customer re-verifies, and `claim_credentials` refreshes memory. The saved card isn't re-charged; the re-verification is the one-time $120 for the cleaning itself.